# Hermes Agent — COMPOSE-LEVEL env only. Copy to .env and fill in.
# The real .env is gitignored and written by the Ubuntu autoinstall at provision
# time (it sets ONLY PANEL_PASSWORD here; PANEL_DOMAIN is left blank to auto-derive).
# NEVER commit a real .env.
#
# IMPORTANT — two separate .env files, do NOT conflate them:
#   * THIS file (/opt/hermes-vm/.env) is the COMPOSE-LEVEL env. docker compose reads
#     it for ${VAR} substitution into the panel + Caddy services. It holds NO
#     provider/Telegram secrets. It is NOT injected into the agent process.
#   * The AGENT'S secrets live in the DATA DIR (./data/.env -> /opt/data/.env) and
#     are written by the panel, not here. Hermes loads ./data/config.yaml +
#     ./data/.env itself at startup; the host applier restarts the agent.

# === CloudHosting setup panel + TLS (compose-level substitution) ===
# Panel login password. REQUIRED — the panel fails closed (refuses to start) if empty.
# Use a strong unique value per VM. This is the ONLY secret the autoinstall sets.
PANEL_PASSWORD=REPLACE_ME
# Public host the panel is served on (TLS via Let's Encrypt). Leave BLANK to have
# firstboot.sh derive it from the primary IPv4 as vps-<3rd octet>-<4th octet>.cloudhosting.lv
# (e.g. 185.8.60.226 -> vps-60-226.cloudhosting.lv). The A-record already exists by
# convention, so HTTP-01 issuance just works. Set it explicitly to override.
PANEL_DOMAIN=

# === File ownership ===
# The agent + panel both run as uid 10000 (hardcoded in docker-compose.yml). No knob
# here — firstboot.sh chowns ./data to 10000 so the panel's 0600 .env is agent-readable.

# === Optional: local admin dashboard (off by default) ===
# Set to 1 AND start the dashboard profile to enable a loopback-only admin UI
# on 127.0.0.1:9119. Reach it via `ssh -L 9119:localhost:9119 <vm>`. Leave unset
# for the smallest attack surface.
# HERMES_DASHBOARD=1

# ===========================================================================
# PROVIDER + TELEGRAM SECRETS ARE *NOT* SET HERE.
# ===========================================================================
# Set these in the panel (admin UI), NOT here — the panel writes them into
# ./data/config.yaml + ./data/.env and restarts the agent via the host applier.
# Specifically, the panel collects and persists into the DATA DIR:
#   * provider + API key   -> ./data/config.yaml (model.provider/base_url/default,
#                             api_key: ${OPENAI_API_KEY}) + ./data/.env
#                             (OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_BASE_URL)
#   * Telegram bot token   -> ./data/.env (TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN)
#   * Telegram allowlist   -> ./data/.env (TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS, comma-separated ids)
# Open https://<PANEL_DOMAIN> after first boot, log in with PANEL_PASSWORD, and enter
# them there. Do NOT add OPENAI_API_KEY / AVOTS_API_KEY / OPENAI_BASE_URL /
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS to THIS compose-level file.
